From: Modulo-Wifi maintainer
Subject: [PATCH] fix(enc28j60): recover from stuck TX state machine (errata #12/#13)

The TX-done handshake relies on the EIR_TXIF interrupt giving tx_ready_sem.
If the ENC28J60 TX state machine latches up (errata #12/#13), TXRTS stays set
and the TX-done interrupt never fires, so tx_ready_sem is never given. The
existing TXERIF recovery in the RX/IRQ task only runs on an interrupt that is
never delivered in this state. The result is that emac_enc28j60_transmit()
times out on tx_ready_sem, then fails the `!(econ1 & ECON1_TXRTS)` check and
returns ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE for every subsequent packet — TX wedges
permanently ("last transmit still in progress" forever), taking down all
outbound traffic while the link still appears up.

Replace the hard abort with an in-line recovery: if TXRTS is still set after
the wait, reset the TX logic (pulse ECON1.TXRST), clear the stale TX interrupt
flags, and continue to transmit the current packet, which re-arms the TX
interrupt and re-asserts TXRTS. This converts a permanent hang into a
self-healing event.

--- a/enc28j60/src/esp_eth_mac_enc28j60.c
+++ b/enc28j60/src/esp_eth_mac_enc28j60.c
@@ -- emac_enc28j60_transmit
     /* ENC28J60 may be a bottle neck in Eth communication. Hence we need to check if it is ready. */
     if (xSemaphoreTake(emac->tx_ready_sem, pdMS_TO_TICKS(ENC28J60_TX_READY_TIMEOUT_MS)) == pdFALSE) {
         ESP_LOGW(TAG, "tx_ready_sem expired");
     }
     MAC_CHECK(enc28j60_do_register_read(emac, true, ENC28J60_ECON1, &econ1) == ESP_OK,
               "read ECON1 failed", out, ESP_FAIL);
-    MAC_CHECK(!(econ1 & ECON1_TXRTS), "last transmit still in progress", out, ESP_ERR_INVALID_STATE);
+    if (econ1 & ECON1_TXRTS) {
+        /* TX state machine is stuck (ENC28J60 errata #12/#13): TXRTS was never
+           cleared and the TX-done interrupt (EIR_TXIF) never fired, so tx_ready_sem
+           was never given. The task's EIR_TXERIF recovery only runs on an interrupt
+           that isn't coming, so without recovery here TX wedges permanently
+           ("last transmit still in progress" forever). Reset the TX state machine,
+           clear the stale TX interrupt flags, and continue with the current packet. */
+        ESP_LOGW(TAG, "TX stuck (TXRTS set); resetting TX state machine");
+        MAC_CHECK(enc28j60_do_bitwise_set(emac, ENC28J60_ECON1, ECON1_TXRST) == ESP_OK,
+                  "set TXRST failed", out, ESP_FAIL);
+        MAC_CHECK(enc28j60_do_bitwise_clr(emac, ENC28J60_ECON1, ECON1_TXRST) == ESP_OK,
+                  "clear TXRST failed", out, ESP_FAIL);
+        MAC_CHECK(enc28j60_do_bitwise_clr(emac, ENC28J60_EIR, EIR_TXERIF | EIR_TXIF) == ESP_OK,
+                  "clear TX interrupt flags failed", out, ESP_FAIL);
+    }
 
     /* Set the write pointer to start of transmit buffer area */
     MAC_CHECK(enc28j60_register_write(emac, ENC28J60_EWRPTL, ENC28J60_BUF_TX_START & 0xFF) == ESP_OK,
               "write EWRPTL failed", out, ESP_FAIL);
